  "description": "An interactive construction tool that teaches students how to bisect any given angle using ruler and compass. In Learn mode, students see a 4-step animated construction: observe the 90° angle, mark equal-distance points A and B via arc from O, draw equal-radius arcs from A and B meeting at C with compass indicators and glow effects, then draw bisector ray OC with SSS congruence overlay. In Practice mode, students answer 12 MCQ questions across 4 categories (concept, calculation, proof, construction) with 3 difficulty levels, shuffled order, explanations on answer, progress tracking, and a results summary. Uses Singularity design system with Poppins font (loaded via <link> tag), #4A4DC9/#FF7212 palette, gradient accents, and CSS keyframes injected via dangerouslySetInnerHTML. Component exported as both named and default export for universal bundler compatibility.",
  "objective_id": "M2.S8.T8.O1",
  "teaching_notes": "Start with 90 degrees since students just learned to construct it. The bisection gives 45 degrees, connecting to the 8-petalled design from the textbook. The congruence overlay in step 4 reinforces the SSS proof: ΔOAC congruent to ΔOBC. In Practice mode, MCQ questions test conceptual understanding, calculation ability, proof reasoning, and construction knowledge. Questions are shuffled each attempt for varied practice. No diagram is shown in Practice mode — students must recall the construction from Learn mode.",
  "implementation_notes": {
    "react_error_130_fixes": [
      "DotGrid converted from bare-array-returning function (buildDotGrid) to a proper React functional component (<DotGrid />) that wraps dots in a Fragment (<>...</>)",
      "EqualMarks returns <g /> (empty SVG group) instead of null when line length < 1, safe for SVG context rendering",
      "Font loaded via <link href=...> element instead of CSS @import inside <style> JSX child string",
      "CSS keyframes and global hover rules injected via <style dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{__html: ...}}> instead of plain JSX string children",
      "HTML entity &amp; in subtitle replaced with JSX string expression for safe rendering"
    ],
    "export_strategy": "Main component declared as plain 'function AngleBisectionConstructor()' with separate 'export { AngleBisectionConstructor }' (named) and 'export default AngleBisectionConstructor' (default) at end of file"
  },
